    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0443",
      "reading_order": 468,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 566.6633068359375,
        "r": 564.7447999999996,
        "b": 531.4631492035388
      },
      "content": "Some generator sets have ground connections to the frame.  Check wiring diagram.  All stator leads must be isolated for testing.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_467",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_7",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_7",
          "title": "7. Generator Set/Regulator Tests"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_467",
          "title": "Testing for Grounds"
        }
      ],
      "page": 40,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0444",
      "reading_order": 469,
      "section": "Testing for Grounds",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 512.5785068359376,
        "r": 564.8393999999996,
        "b": 439.4514492035389
      },
      "content": "Use a megger or insulation resistance meter which applies not more than 500 VDC to the test leads (Figure 7-4).  Test each stator winding for short to laminations.  A reading less than 100,000 ohms indicates a questionable stator. Thoroughly dry the stator and retest.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_467",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_7",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_7",
          "title": "7. Generator Set/Regulator Tests"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_467",
          "title": "Testing for Grounds"
        }
      ],
